  <p>That is why the 2 PM slump feels so familiar. The thing you use to escape the crash keeps setting up the next one.</p>
  <p>I was not looking for another energy drink with a cleaner label.</p>
  <p class="beat">I was looking for a different pattern.</p>

  <h2>Then I learned Kratom was not another coffee drink</h2>
  <p>Kratom comes from <em>Mitragyna speciosa</em>, a tree in the coffee family that grows in Southeast Asia.</p>

  <figure>
    <!--LEAVES-->
    <img src="{{ 'adv-coffee-kratom-leaves.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Glossy green leaves of the Mitragyna speciosa tree in dappled forest light" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy">
    <figcaption><em>Mitragyna speciosa.</em> Same botanical family as coffee. Completely different plant.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>Same botanical family. Completely different plant.</p>
  <p>And unlike caffeine, Kratom is dose-dependent. Smaller amounts tend to produce energy and focus. Larger amounts lean toward body ease and relaxation.</p>

  <div class="dose" role="group" aria-label="How the amount changes the experience">
    <div class="dose__cell"><div class="dose__amt">Smaller amounts</div><p class="dose__what">Tend to produce energy and focus.</p></div>
    <div class="dose__cell"><div class="dose__amt">Larger amounts</div><p class="dose__what">Lean toward body ease and relaxation.</p></div>
  </div>

  <p>That changed how I thought about it.</p>
  <p>I was not choosing between coffee and a different version of coffee. I was looking at a plant with a different range of experiences, depending on the amount.</p>
  <ul class="stack">
    <li>No neon can.</li>
    <li>No third drink to repair the second.</li>
    <li>No promise that I needed to push harder for the rest of the day.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>But there was one problem I expected before I even tried it.</p>

